==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|taglą|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|dek-|lang=ine-pro}}.  Cognate with Middle Low German {{term|tagel||twisted whip|lang=gml}}, Old High German {{term|zagal||animal’s tail|lang=goh}} (dialectical German {{term|Zagel|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|tagl||horse’s or cow’s tail|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐍄𐌰𐌲𐌻||hair of the head|lang=got}}; and, beyond Germanic, with Old Irish {{term|dūal||lock of hair|lang=sga}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtæjel/|lang=ang}}

